The implemented `SymbolSchema` freezes its complete descriptor, rectangle, companion inventory and generated mathematical environment once; CAS validates, sorts and encodes the environment. The schema is immutable and uses shared ownership, independently of the local mutable graph owners of result symbols. Each declaration retains that environment while creating its own graph and exact target relations. Explicit compatibility checks compare every descriptor field with metered structural equality, including exact scale and origin, without printed keys or address identity. A changed name-comparison policy refuses; storage ceilings remain active. Dropping one schema reference cannot invalidate another live reference or an already published result under (`ex:bindings:quantity-registration-environment-scaling`), (`rule:bindings:quantity-registration-freshness`), (`test:integration:frozen-symbol-schema-refuses-incompatible-meaning`), (`test:integration:frozen-symbol-schema-refuses-changed-policy`) and the root decision “Freeze environments before registration reuse”.

