Before signature sharing, failing probes of the frozen path reconfirmed 8,100 caller Work: draft encoding 303, staging 2,445, journal checkpoint 256, six draft visits, policy authentication one, expression/reference checking 3,148, structural-key encoding 964 and index probing 977. The six draft encodings comprise a 17-byte frozen-header reference, three 68-byte Free drafts and two 41-byte relation drafts. Draft bytes and their length depend only on the closed schema and local reference positions, but the current path reconstructs them and still copies metadata into fresh graph records; retaining a byte length alone cannot justify removing the staging allowance. The fixed checkpoint, current storage containment and fresh graph publication remain per-instance obligations under (`ex:bindings:frozen-symbol-work`), (`ex:bindings:quantity-registration-transaction-cost`), (`rule:bindings:quantity-registration-attempt`).

