**Rule (Header-key segment reuse preserves symbol admission)** · `rule:bindings:registration-key-segment`

Symbol admission retains only the existing frozen mathematical signature within a graph's header key. `SymbolSchema` remains the immutable descriptor, rectangle and companion authority; a new context snapshot starts with its own schema slot, and replacing the frozen environment selects that replacement's complete bytes. Descriptor incompatibility still refuses through `declare_for`, changed name policy still refuses at CAS authentication, and all Free membership, sort and ordered companion-target checks still execute. This changes no symbol identity or arithmetic authority under (`dec:bindings:quantity-frozen-environment`), (`rule:bindings:quantity-registration-freshness`), (`rule:bindings:quantity-registration-attempt`) and the root decision “Retain the invariant header-key segment”.

## Physical reading contracts · `sec:bindings:readings`

`readings::CoordinateFamily` admits a declared Real coordinate matrix and every original per-entry meaning. Its expansions retain complete CAS affine definitions, including repeated, negative and structural-zero rows. `EntryMeaning` checks the physical kind, measure, affine role, exact positive reference and optional point origin; independently constructed equal-looking references remain distinct. A mixed state needs no homogeneous buffer descriptor. Reading maps connect compatible coordinates; unlike kinds refuse even when dimensions match, and original conflicting kind declarations cannot disappear under a zero coefficient.

`CoordinateNormalization` retains ordered coherent entry meanings, the exact diagonal restoration and CAS checked inverse, its determinant and both certificates. Positive source-free difference references and explicit point origins retain their original identities. `CoordinateImage` independently checks the diagonal image of normalization, restoration or ordered frame conversion and retains its complete original correspondence key. Exact degree-to-turn cancellation exports `1/360`; any remaining non-rational scale or shift refuses with `UnsupportedExactConstantExport`. Reuse additionally requires the original physical reference identities and the consumer’s live numerical dependencies, format and arithmetic revision. Single-certificate measurement reads the exact canonical length through `VerifiedWitness::exported_byte_len` before export. The consumer retains its conservative eight-byte-per-wire-byte native-witness allowance plus metadata, separately from the temporary copy that CAS export meters itself. Inverse measurement reserves both native witnesses by their actual lengths and drops each temporary export before copying the next. Preflight therefore scales with the certificates actually retained; subsequent numerical evaluation uses those measured retained sizes.

`PhysicalReading::define` retains the returned CAS defined-reading handle as its identity, together with the original symbol, selection expression, ordered entry list, full map and family context. A declaration or display name supplies no equation. `project` builds native Complex components or ordered finite matrix projections. `ReadingRelation::prove` checks both physical endpoints and asks CAS to prove equality on the whole free-coordinate family. `replay` independently reconstructs the full expected judgment, including domain and definedness, before checking portable CAS bytes. Changed copies, signs, order, definitions or domains refuse; a different valid overlapping copy needs its own claim. Physical metadata is independently checked on the receiving side, and is never imported as a theorem from proof bytes.

`ReadingAxis` retains an actual CAS integer index declaration, exact order and complete block boundaries. `ReadingShape` checks ordered axis extents and a total nonoverlapping rectangular partition against the actual matrix reading. These are sealed bindings-owned physical records over CAS handles. CAS owns mathematical shape, maps and equality; physical units, kinds and interpretation remain bindings checks. No new CAS operator or wire field is introduced. Numerical allocation, selected versions, companion coverage and publication remain matrix obligations.

Each budgeted adapter uses the caller's Work ledger, including failed attempts. Temporary metadata is checked before allocation, and proof/export/replay retain the CAS payload and witness limits. Public boundary tests exercise exact `N` success and `N−1` refusal for entry, family, expansion, reading, projection, relation, export, replay, axis and partition operations. The independent replay tests cover mixed state components, Complex real copies, partial overlaps and composition through a common family; they supply no floating payload as a premise.

## Companion, source and representation evidence · `sec:bindings:reading-companions`

`CompanionParameters` declares distinct actual parameter symbols and ordered physical targets. `CompanionReading` defines their exact affine readings: deterministic bounds and numerical errors use `abs(T)*r` over all selected stored copies, while covariance composes the full family maps as `T*U*Q^T`. Covariance keeps both target references, product units and zero offsets. Repeated and negative expansion rows preserve correlation; bounds retain the discrepancy of each selected copy. `CompanionRelation` requires complete ordered physical target equations before proving or replaying the companion equation. `ParameterErrorReading` targets the covariance or bound parameter itself and transports its prior numerical error through the absolute parameter map; matrix must additionally enclose evaluation of that map.

`ParameterErrorReading::check_sources` authenticates the original parameter and parameter-error symbols through complete identity readings. It checks logical order and the source parameter/error units, so an equal-shaped output parameter, another stored selection or a transformed reading cannot be supplied as the input of its own companion map. The numerical owner retains and revalidates both source versions separately from the ordered output targets.

`ReadingSource` names an original free source coordinate. `JointSources` requires a complete ordered triangular inventory of `Known`, `DeclaredZero` or `Unknown` relations, including each diagonal. `Known` blocks target both actual source readings. A declared zero retains an explicit scoped Boolean premise; it is a model assumption, never a theorem of independence. `Unknown` or omitted needed relations refuse. Combining models requires `check_compatible` on every shared source pair. `IndexedReading` checks a homogeneous physical column against its exact index declaration, extent and order; selecting a point preserves the original family and creates no independent source.

`Representation` proves and independently replays a complete reconstruction. `ComponentPair` reconstructs both Complex coordinates; `ComplexBlock` reconstructs all four logical entries `(a,b,-b,a)`, including the unread negative and repeated copies. `Defined` layouts require their own complete exact expansion. `None` requires exact constancy on the whole free family and therefore has no numerical storage obligation; an unresolved varying input cannot become `None`. These equations concern exact targets. Numerical admission of every rounded copy, its family enclosure, and all imported/evaluated companion errors remain matrix obligations.

`project_selected` and `ProjectionSpace::Selected` name original selected storage coordinates, while `project` names logical result coordinates. A Complex block therefore retains four storage coordinates even though its reading has two logical coordinates. Exact Work and staged-payload boundaries cover family composition, companion parameter/read/error construction, companion proof/replay, representation proof/replay, source models and indexed grids; the allocation-free source compatibility scan has Work boundaries and succeeds with zero staged payload. Existing scalar pairing derivation retains its own bounded descriptor-arithmetic ledger, as in `src/pairing/`; no budget is raised for acceptance.

## Exact operation contracts · `sec:bindings:reading-operations`

`AffineOperation` proves or independently replays a result reading against an exact map rebuilt over its original input. Copy and component projection are identity and selection instances of this contract; another result symbol, map, kind, origin or family cannot substitute. `LinearOperator` declares an actual Real matrix with ordered domain/codomain axes and formal output/input coefficient meanings, including every typed zero. `OperatorCoefficient` retains both coordinate references and the exact quotient of their coherent magnitudes; it invents no scalar quotient kind and makes no derivative claim.

`OperatorApplication` constructs native ordered CAS `MatrixMultiply` syntax as the result definition. The result identity is that actual expression, with its ordered operands, result axes and per-entry meanings. Its CAS witness checks definedness on the retained domain, and fresh replay rebuilds the whole expected judgment independently; an unresolved domain refuses. This supplies an exact operation requirement for a numerical client. It proves no independent Free-output equation, reassociation, Complex block product correspondence or numerical enclosure theorem. Those lowerings retain their separate obligations. `readings::algebra` reexports the exact construction API so consumers need no extra dependency to name these endpoints.

`PhasorBlockCorrespondence` checks the closed identity `R(z*w)=R(z)*R(w)` componentwise over the actual real/imaginary reading projections. Exact rational distribution compares all four ordered coefficient rows; the retained bilinear basis names products of those projections and introduces no independent source declaration. Native Complex and ordered Real product syntax, all four native entry equations and both complete representation witnesses remain together. Exact rational composition checks each full-family conjugation/transpose equation against the retained reconstruction witness, avoiding repeated graph-wide proof construction. The closed LC convention uses passive signs and the positive time exponent; another convention, reordered operand or selected reading refuses. This coordinate law supplies neither physical result units nor a solve-domain, norm-transfer or numerical enclosure certificate. The native CAS matrix coefficient producer still refuses projections of Complex readings inside the block product, so the multiplication correspondence is the bindings-owned closed component check.

`PhasorSolveDefinition` prescribes the original physical equation `Z*I=V` using the checked multiplication correspondence and a fresh current block. It checks the registered impedance/current product kind against voltage and proves the real impedance coordinate identically zero on the original family. It retains every proved fixed input component, including exact zeros, for independent numerical import coverage. It grants no invertibility premise. `PhasorResidualTransfer` retains uniform positive voltage/current component metrics and their reference identities. The exact induced operator two-norm is `abs(X)*I_ref/V_ref`; the block Frobenius norm is `sqrt(2)` times this value. Reconstructed block residuals likewise carry a `sqrt(2)` factor relative to component residuals. Numerical separation, input-copy errors and the actual solve theorem remain matrix obligations; an arbitrary rounded block residual cannot inherit the reconstructed-block factor.

`PhasorCovarianceLaw` derives the exact affine current gains from two checked equations with fixed, nonzero imaginary impedances and one original voltage family. Both complete source maps, including selections and repeated copies, enter the signed two-sided covariance law. `CompanionReading::phasor_covariance` transports the original voltage covariance into the actual current target units through these retained equations; it refuses a varying impedance or an independent replacement voltage source. Offsets affect the means but do not create covariance sources.

`PositiveReciprocalMap` checks a closed coefficient recipe `map(reference[i]/input[i])` against an independently supplied original exact operator. Distinct formal Real inputs retain their ordered coherent difference meanings and source-free positive references; the coefficient map has exact rational mixing coefficients and offsets in logical column order. Original syntax is checked before reduction: total polynomial and explicit matrix arithmetic are admitted, while division requires a formal positive input or a nonzero rational literal. Cancelled denominators and unused inputs retain their obligations. The native exact image, original operator, reciprocal temporary definitions, complete correspondence witness and authenticated reuse key remain together. Numerical consumers bind every formal slot, prove strict positivity over every full input box, and preserve the exact recipe beside numerical versions and arithmetic identity. This contract supplies no statistical propagation or numerical sign premise. Witness retention preflights actual `VerifiedWitness::exported_byte_len` values before metered export; no fixed witness ceiling substitutes for the measured length. The public LC fixture pins construction at 879,328 Work, 134,652 staged bytes and 45,762 output bytes, with exact success/refusal boundaries and cumulative caller charges.

`PositiveReciprocalMap::allocation` derives a closed storage-neutral `ReciprocalAllocation` from the retained exact declaration without constructing another CAS graph. `ReciprocalStage` fixes every finite kernel buffer and `ReciprocalComponent` distinguishes imported candidates, constant endpoints, import displacement, total and nominal image endpoints and result radii. `ReciprocalEntry` resolves each logical target to its original physical reference, exact rational coefficient, reciprocal expression or selected output expression. Different physical references remain different entry meanings even when packed together. Shared-declaration identity and stage determine allocation-binding equality; an out-of-range entry has no declared meaning. Matrix supplies opaque numerical tickets, concrete representation checks and live publication coverage; the bindings record alone grants no storage access. This implements the closed reciprocal scratch subset of `docs/design/descriptor-binding.md`; solve and general scratch bindings remain separate obligations.

`ReciprocalJacobianKey` prepares the native source-derivative identity from the checked original homogeneous operator, its complete context and ordered physical inputs. Explicit fixed inputs remain in the original positive-domain obligations and introduce no derivative column. `ReciprocalJacobianCache` retains one shared derivative bundle per exact mathematical and physical key, including the original-to-explicit representation witness. Compatible uses compare actual key bytes and shared immutable physical declarations; a hit creates no graph records and replays no proof. Independent reference identities cannot substitute even when descriptions and numerical values agree. This adapter operates on the caller's existing CAS graph and never constructs a per-request context or budget.

Recipe construction, key admission, native derivation and cache reuse all take the same caller `Budget`. `SourceJacobianUsage` preserves complete before/after `BudgetUsage` snapshots, while failed attempts remain charged in the caller ledger. Both the permanent CAS policy and caller policy must explicitly cover the entire pipeline, because CAS intersects every ceiling. The LC source fixture costs 879,328 Work for its recipe, 381,309 for its key, 4,986,140 for native derivation with checking and replay, and 7,579 for a cache hit; with 17 prior Work its complete boundary is 6,254,373/7,305,264. Retained derivative evidence occupies a conservative 108,158 bytes. Separate audits export the 1,981-byte representation and 3,796-byte derivative witnesses and replay them fresh for 712,637 and 965,024 Work respectively; these audits do not split the native producer's internal ledger. The fixed-C and all-fixed requests cost 3,996,054 and 3,053,317 Work on their shared graph; the complete variant, including recipe construction and invalid/foreign requests, consumes 8,574,487 Work under its own explicit policy. The all-fixed request retains original-domain and representation evidence without derivative columns. Numerical operating points and covariance claims remain separate from the exact derivative key.

`RootProblem::check` retains a complete original solve request, its occurrence roots and sealed traversal receipts, and delegates predicate and ordered divisor validation to CAS. `RootCoverage::replay` reconstructs the expected coverage judgment from that admitted problem, its exact context and the proposed set before independently replaying the portable witness. The original LC determinant keeps separate positive L/C guards, nested family bodies and all four divisor occurrences; a reduced polynomial or sampled parameter pair cannot replace that request. The adapter retains the original request and full root/factor witness together. Physical interpretation, similarity transport and numerical root enclosures remain separate obligations.

`RootCoverage` takes one caller-owned cumulative `Budget`, with explicit Work and replay allowances for the original LC theorem, and never creates a default ledger. `RootReplayUsage` records every usage counter before expected-claim construction, before replay and after success; failed attempts retain their charges in the caller ledger. Native request and witness storage is reserved through `with_retained_payload`, and later consumers can reserve the exposed retained size beside other live evidence. Request search overrides remain documentary generation policy and do not select replay allowances.

The original LC public fixture costs 826,907 Work to construct and 4,468 Work to admit as a `RootProblem`; upstream generation remains 809,206 Work. Because the CAS family exclusions share checked nonzero leaves, a proof-free receiver requires 1,433,783 replay Work plus one Work to construct its expected judgment, with exact 1,433,784/1,433,783 caller-Work and 1,433,783/1,433,782 replay boundaries. Reusing the populated proof store costs 1,431,770 replay Work. Single-pass replay reuses the checked canonical encoding. Fresh replay fits under the default 2,000,000 Work ceiling; the repeated-request ladder with 17 prior Work requires 2,865,572, with exact 2,865,572/2,865,571 success/refusal and charged retries. Admission, replay and export with 19 prior Work require 1,444,411 on one ledger. The 6,140-byte portable witness retains a conservative 52,448-byte native payload and requires 352,789 staged bytes during replay, about 57 times the wire size. Those storage allowances include replay machinery and retained originals; they are measured for this proof representation and are not wire-size limits. Exact storage boundaries, cumulative admission/export and repeated replay/refusal tests pin the current implementation without changing defaults.

`LcSpectralLaw` checks the original LC determinant against the independently replayed complete-root theorem, including the original positive L/C stratum, its family projection and the unrestricted Complex unknown domain. An explicit ordered parameter transport checks the original independent Real base against the physical recipe inputs in a separate real context; both complete domains contain exactly the positive L/C guards. It authenticates all original determinant operands and both parameter identities, without equating distinct headers or matching display names. Original root coverage is unconditional. The transport correspondence retains its named positivity assumptions visibly through `transport_hypotheses`; `is_unconditional` reports them honestly, while numerical execution proves strict positivity over both complete input boxes. The whole reciprocal coefficient map must be exactly `[[0,a],[-b,0]]`, with positive coefficient factors and identically zero diagonals on the entire family. The ordered coherent `voltage`, `current`, `inductance`, `capacitance` and `duration` kinds retain their exact dimensions and source-free references. Exact coefficient comparison proves `B=t_ref*S^(-1)*A*S`; changing a state or time reference requires checking another transport. The original two native root selections remain retained as an unordered pair; positivity makes both characteristic factors simple, while matrix assigns positive/negative imaginary numerical enclosures only after its full-box guards. A solve residual, center-only zero pattern, omitted root or arbitrary row/column scaling cannot supply this contract. The checked transport costs 66,696 Work and owns 832 bytes; its native hypothesis authentication peaks at 17,344 staged bytes. The independent physical fixture construction costs 1,557,249 Work under the unchanged 2,000,000 default, separately from original root replay.

`LcRootJacobian` joins one `LcSpectralLaw` to the same cached `ReciprocalJacobian` used by the original operator. It checks the original operator key, ordered formal inputs, physical context and reference identities, and complete derivative-direction coverage. The retained positive characteristic identity gives `d(r/t_ref)=(b*da+a*db)/(2*r*t_ref)` for `r=sqrt(a*b)>0`; the negative imaginary root has the opposite derivative and both real derivatives vanish. The adapter shares the original exact proof without another cache lookup, derivation or replay. Its admission costs 4797 Work and 632 staged/output bytes, with exact and one-below boundaries. Numerical consumers must still revalidate the original operating point and model, enclose this schedule and retain first-order statistical assurance. This contract grants no nonlinear moments or deterministic support.

`LcSpectralResultDefinition` predeclares the positive and negative Complex roots, both Real parts and both imaginary parts. Its fresh output header has an unrestricted context with no assumptions, checked in the same CAS as the physical law. This keeps unrelated output declarations out of the immutable physical proof header. It checks all six exact maps over one shared positive rate coordinate, keeps the proved real zeros as `None`, authenticates each logical component projection and retains the complete original spectral law. Every nonzero component and conjugate view shares entries through checked signed reading maps. The output kind is the derivative/eigenvalue `rate` in inverse seconds, with a unit reference; angular and cyclic frequency remain separate quantities. The result definition costs 13,763 Work with a 227,968-byte retained allowance; its shared original law and coordinate meanings are excluded, while ten distinct native witnesses use the established conservative envelope because their allocation capacities are not public.

The read-only matrix adapters in `crates/matrix/src/binding/adapters/` consume these definitions, representation witnesses, exact companion targets and selected-coordinate overlap equations. They carry opaque tickets rather than resolve heap handles. A planned numerical result must match the exact result definition, axes, references, selection and companion/source inventory, and the numerical owner must separately validate every live version and enclosure before execution or publication.

