Public conformance tests exercise dimensional/kind/role refusals, exact scale identities, original invalid operands hidden by zero, stale snapshots, companion identities and missing premises. Integration tests cover exact frequency round trips, constant export, schema maps and symbolic sensitivity lifecycles. Admission tests pin exact entry limits and cumulative CAS `N`/`N−1` boundaries; sensitivity tests measure each fixture's required work afresh and check exact-limit success and one-below refusal. Compile twins protect checked pairing state. Run `cargo test -p nrz-bindings --test public` for the public contract; rustdoc checks the front-page example and included compile twins. Bindings test evidence establishes the declared exact fragment; the separate matrix tests in the LC route table establish its supported numerical consumers.

`ParameterSymbol` declares a complete per-entry mathematical parameter inventory. Entries retain actual value/source coordinates, checked covariance or sensitivity pairings, or exact parameter-error targets. `BindingSymbols::from_reading` admits only coherent homogeneous identity-coordinate readings for closed recipes. `with_reading_companions` attaches the original identity-map radius definitions to a scalar or column reading, checks exact targets and distinct kinds, and requires a total whenever numerical error is present. It preserves the original companion nodes and refuses covariance and nonidentity maps. Companion comparison traverses the already authenticated value map on the caller ledger; it does not reconstruct an identity map. A fresh copy retains the actual source declaration and selected reading lineage even when its immutable graph authority differs. These sealed physical records grant no numerical storage access.

`BindingSymbols::restored_reading` checks a homogeneous projection against the original mixed identity reading, including its family, selected positions, complete entry meanings and fixed reference identities. It declares a fresh result with both radius channels and retains the original component through its source edge. These derived symbols refuse ordinary import: matrix must execute restoration, retain the original companions and publish the checked channels together. Physical metadata supplies no floating values or increased assurance. The restoration contract is in `docs/design/lc-resonance.md`.

`PhasorResultDefinition` associates one fresh output storage family with the actual checked native product and an explicitly registered coherent physical product kind. The fresh root is an output slot initialized only by that operation, rather than an assumed input equality. Its reconstruction law covers every repeated and negated result entry. Numerical publication must retain the operation and all original source versions; this declaration alone initializes no values.

